OL,3,GNEWSA'The phone is my elderly mum's    
OL,4,Alifeline, but cable thefts have left   
OL,5,Aher isolated'                          
OL,7,FAt 93 years old, Madge has always been 
OL,8,F"fiercely independent", but after      
OL,9,Fcopper cables were stolen from near her
OL,10,Fhome, she has been left "isolated" and 
OL,11,F"vulnerable", according to daughter    
OL,12,FHelen.                                 
OL,14,FMadge, from east Leeds, is just one of 
OL,15,Fmany individuals and business owners   
OL,16,Facross West Yorkshire who have been    
OL,17,Fleft without their phones or internet  
OL,18,Fas cases of copper thefts climb.       
OL,20,F"It is her lifeline," Helen says of her
OL,21,Fmum's telephone.                       
